{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6b90abf8-385c-44a5-9c34-eeb6aba8bde3","agentId":"aae06db009bbe4b77","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"No subagents/forks, no commits/pushes, no searching, no screenshots. Report under 120 words. Spec: C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\research\\JOB_UX_FIXES_2026-10-08.md items 1, 2, 3, 4, 10, 11 (data side). Files: mes-log-mcp/mes/jobs.py, cuore/live/checklists.py, cuore/api/jobs.py, cuore/api/checklists.py, cuore/services/jobs_bridge.py, cuore/services/flow_bridge.py, cuore/tests/check_jobs_rules.py (new), mes-log-mcp/server.py (tool updates only). Do not edit templates, jobs_routes.py, bench_*, _vbar, cuore.css (other agents). Repo C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers; Python .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe; tests use a temp CUORE_STATE_DIR; VIN ZASFAKPN5J7B88115.\n\nContract the page agent codes against (keep these names):\n1. Hypothesis status path: open -> supported -> confirmed; refuted allowed from any state; `set_hypothesis(job_id, hyp_id, status, by=None)` raises `RuleViolation(reason, next_test)` -> HTTP 409 {\"detail\": reason, \"next_test\": ...} when: confirmed without >=1 evidence_for ref of kind \"test\" whose result is pass or fail, or with any unresolved evidence_against (ref without `resolved: true`), or jumping open -> confirmed. Store confirmed_by/confirmed_at and an `audit` list [{at, by, action, detail}] per hypothesis.\n2. Evidence: `add_evidence(job_id, hyp_id, side: for|against, ref)` and `remove_evidence(...)`; ref = {kind: code|freeze_frame|live|test|observation, id, label, result?, resolved?}; `edit_hypothesis(job_id, hyp_id, text=None, system=None, codes=None, likelihood=None, next_test=None)`; `delete_hypothesis(job_id, hyp_id)` soft-delete with `deleted: true` and `undelete`. New fields on a hypothesis: codes: [], likelihood: low|med|high|None, updated_at, deleted.\n3. Test results: checklist entries gain `result: pass|fail|inconclusive|not_possible|None`, `reason`, `value`, `unit`, `hypothesis_id`, `media_ids`; `set_result(vin, step_id, result, ...)` and, when hypothesis_id is given, automatically adds an evidence ref {kind: \"test\", id: step_id, label: \"<step text>: <result> <value><unit>\", result} to that hypothesis (for on pass/fail per its `supports: for|against` arg; default for). Only pass/fail count as test evidence.\n4. Step states in flow_bridge: every step gets `state: not_started|in_progress|complete` and `progress: {done, total}` from real criteria (step 6: checklist rows with a result over all rows; step 7: hypotheses with status != open over hypotheses; step 5: viewed cannot be known: count codes with a feel/experience entry opened? No: step 5 complete when at least one hypothesis exists OR the user marked \"understood\" via an explicit action; not_started otherwise); never green with 0 done. Keep `status` for the old consumers but derive it from state.\n5. jobs_bridge.suggested_hypotheses: deduplicate suggestions that share the same next_test into one card listing the affected codes (\"Upstream check: Network/CAN: B1029, B102E, ...\"), rank by evidence_for count then likelihood, return `top` (3) and `rest`; `similar_existing(job, text, system)` -> the most similar existing hypothesis (token overlap >= 0.5) for the merge prompt.\n6. API (cuore/api/jobs.py): POST .../hypotheses/{id}/status (409 on rule violation with detail+next_test), POST .../hypotheses/{id}/evidence (add/remove), POST .../hypotheses/{id} (edit), DELETE/undelete, POST /api/vehicles/{vin}/checklist/{step_id}/result; a `step_registry()` with ids/titles for cross references (item 10) exposed from flow_bridge. Tests (6): open->confirmed is 409 with next_test; pass test linked -> supported allowed -> confirmed allowed with by/at recorded; evidence_against unresolved blocks confirm; soft delete + undelete; step 6 state not_started 0/N with no results and in_progress after one; suggestions dedupe reduces 8 identical upstream checks to 1 with the codes listed. Run + cuore/tests/check_jobs_page.py, check_flow.py, check_bench.py."},"uuid":"230df37c-e699-4948-8632-8d123d965ea7","timestamp":"2026-10-08T18:52:43.798Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
