{"parentUuid":"598f88f4-5aec-479a-a5f1-cd380e9db4b5","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aae06db009bbe4b77","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfqKQ7gsL9JSBPHJrGqjc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UozqaEbnUp3KavxDRfPZPR","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\tests\\check_cases.py","limit":40},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1150,"cache_read_input_tokens":239067,"output_tokens":146,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1150},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":146,"cache_read_input_tokens":239067,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1150,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1150,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01UozqaEbnUp3KavxDRfPZPR":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\tests\\check_cases.py","limit":40}},"serverClassifierRequest":"7f8e1748-232b-4337-9b61-4ff021bcc7d8","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfqKQ7PmoK6ZWtnAMwtvR","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"464db38a-dfb6-4841-8587-810719d79ad0","timestamp":"2026-10-08T19:25:15.291Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"464db38a-dfb6-4841-8587-810719d79ad0","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0dafa9fa-5929-4c31-b2e6-0bfc53bbb280","agentId":"aae06db009bbe4b77","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UozqaEbnUp3KavxDRfPZPR","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Checks for case memory: ``mes.cases`` (``case_from_job``, ``match``,\n2\t``prefill``) and its thin pass-throughs in ``cuore.services.cases_bridge``.\n3\t\n4\t``CUORE_STATE_DIR`` is pointed at a fresh tempdir BEFORE anything cuore/mes\n5\tis imported, so this never touches the real state directory (which, as of\n6\tthis change, carries one real seeded case for the project Stelvio -- see\n7\t``mes.cases.seed_default``). Every fixture job here is built directly\n8\tthrough ``mes.jobs``/``mes.tool_usage``, same as ``check_jobs_page.py``'s\n9\tfixtures, so each case is built from a real (if synthetic-for-the-test) job\n10\trecord, never hand-written.\n11\t\n12\t``cuore/api/cases.py`` is not registered on ``cuore.app.create_app`` (this\n13\ttask's scope excludes ``app.py``), so wording/ranking checks go straight\n14\tthrough ``mes.cases`` and ``cuore.services.cases_bridge`` rather than HTTP --\n15\tsame posture as the module itself being the one place every rule (code\n16\toverlap, \"never proven\" wording) actually lives.\n17\t\n18\tFive checks:\n19\t  1. ``case_from_job`` builds a case from a fixture job with actions and a\n20\t     tool-usage review (codes, tools used, and a path all land).\n21\t  2. ``match`` ranks the case whose codes overlap the query first.\n22\t  3. ``prefill`` returns hypotheses, tools and pitfalls from the matched case.\n23\t  4. Every wording surface says \"last Stelvio\" (or the model name) and\n24\t     never \"proven\".\n25\t  5. A VIN that doesn't resolve to the Stelvio model gets no matches, even\n26\t     though Stelvio cases are on file.\n27\t\n28\tRun:\n29\t    .venv/Scripts/python.exe cuore/tests/check_cases.py\n30\t\"\"\"\n31\t\n32\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n33\t\n34\timport json\n35\timport os\n36\timport sys\n37\timport tempfile\n38\tfrom pathlib import Path\n39\t\n40\tos.environ[\"CUORE_STATE_DIR\"] = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"cuore-check-cases-\")"}]},"uuid":"33654692-81a2-4227-8ee2-91b90042d0f6","timestamp":"2026-10-08T19:25:15.333Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\tests\\check_cases.py","content":"\"\"\"Checks for case memory: ``mes.cases`` (``case_from_job``, ``match``,\n``prefill``) and its thin pass-throughs in ``cuore.services.cases_bridge``.\n\n``CUORE_STATE_DIR`` is pointed at a fresh tempdir BEFORE anything cuore/mes\nis imported, so this never touches the real state directory (which, as of\nthis change, carries one real seeded case for the project Stelvio -- see\n``mes.cases.seed_default``). Every fixture job here is built directly\nthrough ``mes.jobs``/``mes.tool_usage``, same as ``check_jobs_page.py``'s\nfixtures, so each case is built from a real (if synthetic-for-the-test) job\nrecord, never hand-written.\n\n``cuore/api/cases.py`` is not registered on ``cuore.app.create_app`` (this\ntask's scope excludes ``app.py``), so wording/ranking checks go straight\nthrough ``mes.cases`` and ``cuore.services.cases_bridge`` rather than HTTP --\nsame posture as the module itself being the one place every rule (code\noverlap, \"never proven\" wording) actually lives.\n\nFive checks:\n  1. ``case_from_job`` builds a case from a fixture job with actions and a\n     tool-usage review (codes, tools used, and a path all land).\n  2. ``match`` ranks the case whose codes overlap the query first.\n  3. ``prefill`` returns hypotheses, tools and pitfalls from the matched case.\n  4. Every wording surface says \"last Stelvio\" (or the model name) and\n     never \"proven\".\n  5. A VIN that doesn't resolve to the Stelvio model gets no matches, even\n     though Stelvio cases are on file.\n\nRun:\n    .venv/Scripts/python.exe cuore/tests/check_cases.py\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nimport os\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nos.environ[\"CUORE_STATE_DIR\"] = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"cuore-check-cases-\")","numLines":40,"startLine":1,"totalLines":166}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"464db38a-dfb6-4841-8587-810719d79ad0","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
