{"parentUuid":"ea1fa18a-35f6-4a6d-bb72-6d81594e5ed5","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aae06db009bbe4b77","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfqLAarjPw3MfK4JVHcG9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01H84gq8h9hQcnTHTbFWwq8f","name":"SubagentHandback","input":{"message":"Implemented items 1, 2, 3, 4, 10, 11 (data side) from JOB_UX_FIXES_2026-10-08.md. All target suites pass: check_jobs_rules.py (27/27, new), check_flow.py (15/15), check_jobs_page.py (24/24), check_bench.py (59/59). Also spot-checked check_flow_bar.py, check_liveboard.py, check_cases.py (all green) since they touch mes.jobs/jobs_bridge.\n\nFiles changed:\n- C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\mes-log-mcp\\mes\\jobs.py — full rewrite. Added `RuleViolation(reason, next_test)`; guided status path enforced in `set_hypothesis` (`open->supported->confirmed`, `refuted` from any state, jump/no-evidence/unresolved-against all raise `RuleViolation`). New: `edit_hypothesis`, `delete_hypothesis`/`undelete_hypothesis` (soft delete), `add_evidence`/`remove_evidence`/`resolve_evidence`. Hypotheses gained `codes`, `likelihood`, `updated_at`, `deleted`, `confirmed_by`, `confirmed_at`, `audit` (list of `{at,by,action,detail}`). `REF_KINDS` extended with `test`/`observation`. `attach`/`add_hypothesis` gained `by`. `ACTION_KINDS` gained `understand`.\n- C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\live\\checklists.py — added `set_result(vin, step_id, result, reason, value, unit, hypothesis_id, media_ids, by)`, merging onto the same per-step entry `set_step` writes (neither clobbers the other's fields).\n- C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\services\\jobs_bridge.py — thin wrappers for all new mes.jobs calls (RuleViolation passed through unconverted from `set_hypothesis`); `dedupe_suggestions`/`rank_suggestions`/`grouped_suggestions` (top 3 + rest); `similar_existing`/`check_similar` (token-overlap >=0.5 merge prompt); `add_test_evidence` (checklist→hypothesis auto-evidence wiring); `step_registry()` re-export from flow_bridge. `suggested_hypotheses` now dedupes+ranks before returning (same flat-list shape, so existing consumers/tests are unaffected). `build_job_view` now also returns `suggested_hypotheses_top/_rest` and `step_registry`.\n- C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\services\\flow_bridge.py — every step dict gained `state` (not_started|in_progress|complete) and `progress` {done,total}; steps 5/6/7 use real criteria (step 5: hypothesis exists or `kind=\"understand\"` action; step 6: checklist rows with a non-null `result`; step 7: non-deleted hypotheses with status != open), never \"complete\" with 0 done. `status` is now derived from `state`. Added `step_registry()`/`step_link(key)`.\n- C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\api\\jobs.py — new/changed routes: `POST .../hypotheses/{id}/status` (409 body `{\"detail\",\"next_test\"}` at top level via plain `JSONResponse`, not HTTPException's nested envelope), `POST .../hypotheses/{id}/evidence` (add/remove/resolve), `POST .../hypotheses/{id}` repurposed as edit, `DELETE .../hypotheses/{id}` + `POST .../undelete`, `GET .../hypotheses/similar`, `GET /jobs/steps`.\n- C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\api\\checklists.py — new `POST /vehicles/{vin}/checklist/{step_id}/result`, auto-attaching `kind=\"test\"` evidence to a named hypothesis on pass/fail.\n- C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\mes-log-mcp\\server.py — added tools `job_add_hypothesis`, `job_edit_hypothesis`, `job_delete_hypothesis`, `job_undelete_hypothesis`, `job_add_evidence`, `job_remove_evidence`; `job_set_hypothesis` now returns a structured `{\"error\":\"RuleViolation\",\"message\",\"next_test\"}` instead of a bare exception string.\n- C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\tests\\check_jobs_rules.py — new, 27 checks covering all 6 required scenarios (409 on jump, pass-test→supported→confirmed with by/at, unresolved-against blocks confirm, soft delete/undelete, step 6 tri-state with real corpus checklist counts, suggestion dedupe of 8→1 with codes listed).\n- C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\tests\\check_flow.py — updated checks 3/4 fixtures: direct `open->confirmed` calls now go through the legal `add_evidence`→`supported`→`confirmed` path (required once the rule is enforced); also mocks `checklist_step_ids` + seeds one passed checklist result so step 6 completes for these synthetic VINs, since step 6 now requires a real checklist row with a result rather than any inspection/observation.\n\nNot touched (per scope): templates, jobs_routes.py, bench_*, _vbar, cuore.css, dossier_bridge.py (only called its existing public `build_view`/`checklist_step_ids`, never edited). cuore/app.py also untouched — `jobs_api.router` and `checklists_api.router` were already mounted there.\n\nOne thing other agents (templates/jobs_routes.py) should know: `jobs_routes.py`'s HTML form `POST /v/{vin}/job/{job_id}/hypotheses/{hyp_id}/status` calls `jobs_bridge.set_hypothesis` directly and does not currently catch `RuleViolation` — on a rule violation that call will propagate as an unhandled exception (no app.py handler registered for it) unless/until that route is updated to catch `jobs_bridge.RuleViolation` and re-render the page with the reason/next_test, mirroring how `job_close` already catches `BridgeError`."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":291,"cache_read_input_tokens":262123,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":291,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01H84gq8h9hQcnTHTbFWwq8f":{"message":"Implemented items 1, 2, 3, 4, 10, 11 (data side) from JOB_UX_FIXES_2026-10-08.md. All target suites pass: check_jobs_rules.py (27/27, new), check_flow.py (15/15), check_jobs_page.py (24/24), check_bench.py (59/59).